        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2b482bf875d14c578aa5c20eb571478d",
      "statement": "The OpenAI embedder batches inputs in fixed groups of 100 (BATCH_SIZE), issuing one client.embeddings.create({ model, input: batch }) call per batch and flattening the returned vectors into a single ordered number[][].",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/indexing/embed.ts#L10-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6ebf544146bbcc9dd648e498f2636862205768036fe46e09ae9a9fc5f86f9d95:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/indexing/embed.ts#L45-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5ee233ed6d98fd5412bc343158aac356fa1db1a9653656b44c82b44f9d3eb99:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_13ae4339157142c0a2c269db73789327",
      "statement": "Each batched OpenAI call is wrapped in a retry helper with MAX_RETRIES=3 total attempts. Retries occur only for HTTP status 429 or status >= 500, using exponential backoff (delay = 2^i * 1000 ms: 1s, 2s, 4s) and a warning log per attempt. All other errors (non-429, status < 500, or missing status) are rethrown immediately; exhausting attempts throws the last error.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/indexing/embed.ts#L13-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:10d28af49c70609838901aab4ddfc7ad1bb2c605ae76b9df0a5e0a881868c847:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/indexing/embed.ts#L49-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:752d062653f8ef05c87d502b7662e36beaeefc280f921e39474a09b69919d089:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0064ceb7bed34953b8a0ab7ba1db3c74",
      "statement": "The embedding model name participates in the content-hash/cache-key computation: hash.ts joins sorted chunk texts, PIPELINE_VERSION (\"1\"), and the model string into a SHA-256 payload. Because index.ts computes contentHash(allChunks, embedder.model), changing the embedding model changes the hash, causing a cache miss and forcing a full re-embed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/index.ts#L31-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bf93a2b7b7826e771d163abad986c5d2f3e4c3c0dda49c9b829a20e9cf5a3693:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/indexing/hash.ts#L4-L9",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b9e597c9fccdf8877bb586ba00b57a6c8e89993cbeaacca48d7ffcee773f8814:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_99ff448ced694208ba245d8a910ae857",
      "statement": "At startup index.ts creates the embedder, computes the content hash from its model, attempts to load a cached VectorStore from DATA_DIR keyed by that hash, and only on a miss calls store.build(allChunks, embedder) (which normalizes vectors to unit length) and persists the result. The same embedder is then passed to buildMcpServer so queries are embedded against the same model used to build the index.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/index.ts#L30-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e51f689260fa955af7a55cc2379b36ee6c12ff8776fc36a45bd67c0603481ce:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/indexing/store.ts#L33-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d85df1c5846dfb0e15228e06f7bc3010767abd567d376a744d78f5f73a7942b8:"
        }
      ]
    }
